menu "Iridium ACARS app options"

config SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    bool "Run target-side smoke test instead of USB streaming"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, app_main runs smoke_test_run() instead of starting
        the USB host daemon and class_driver tasks. The smoke test feeds
        a synthetic noise/tone/noise IQ stream through the production
        ingest -> dsp_processor path and asserts the FFT detector raises
        a burst at the expected bin with high SNR.

        Use for functional regression checks before/after changes that
        touch the convert, signal_buffer, ingest_core1, or dsp_processor
        code. No USB device needs to be attached.

config SMOKE_TEST_CORPUS
    bool "Use the test_corpus fixture (real Iridium burst) instead of a synthetic tone"
    depends on SMOKE_TEST_MODE
    default n
    help
        When enabled, the smoke test uses tests/fixtures/fixture_corpus_uint8.h
        as the signal source — a real Iridium burst from
        test_corpus/prbs15-2M-20dB.sigmf-data, resampled to 2.56 MSPS and
        quantised to uint8 IQ. The detector should fire on the burst's
        carrier (FFT bin near DC since the corpus carrier is at the SDR
        center frequency).

        The fixture must be regenerated via tests/scripts/build_fixtures.py
        if the corpus or resampling parameters change. Without this flag,
        the smoke test uses a synthetic tone at FFT bin 200 (semantic
        regression check, not a corpus regression).

endmenu
